            <ArticleTitle>Transoesophageal echocardiography in diagnosis of aberrant coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aberrant origin of the main stem of the left coronary artery from the right sinus of Valsalva caused angina of effort in a 40 year-old patient. Diagnosis was revealed by transoesophageal echocardiography and confirmed by selective coronary angiography. Aorto-coronary bypass was performed in order to prevent the recurrence of myocardial ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
